Sentinelle
==========

Sentinelle is a derivative work based on Saracroche, an open-source Android
call- and SMS-spam blocking application created by cbouvat.

Original project:
  Name:      Saracroche
  Author:    cbouvat
  Source:    https://codeberg.org/cbouvat/saracroche-android
  License:   GNU General Public License v3.0

Sentinelle forked the Saracroche codebase at version 5.1.1 and, in
accordance with the terms of the GNU General Public License v3.0, is
licensed as a whole under the same license (see LICENSE). The complete,
unmodified license text is preserved in this repository.

Summary of changes made since the fork:
  - Renamed the application and its package identifier from
    "Saracroche" (com.cbouvat.android.saracroche) to
    "Sentinelle" (com.sentinelle.app).
  - Added a unified blocked-event history covering both calls and SMS,
    and a statistics/history dashboard.
  - Added an on-device, rule-based (heuristic) spam-scoring module, with
    an abstraction designed to later accommodate a trained on-device
    machine-learning model.

